WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:07.140
GAL VERED: Hello,
everyone, and thank you

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.860
for joining this session focused
on making business calls safer

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.850
and more effective
with verified calls.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:14.770
My name is Gal.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.650
I'm a product manager
at Google, and I'm

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:23.070
joined by my teammate Stephen,
who leads our partnerships.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.230
Let me kick things off by
sharing a personal story.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.220
Last month, my bank tried
to call me several times

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.330
about the potential fraudulent
activity on my account.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.490
But to be honest,
I just missed those

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:43.220
calls in the sea of spam calls
that I receive every day, I

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.450
only realized that something
was wrong after a week when

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.670
I tried to use my credit
card and it declined.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.060
Now, luckily, I
had a spare card,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.310
so no big damage was done.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.760
But you can imagine how
stressful the situation

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.080
might have been with slightly
different circumstances.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.860
And this story
puts the spotlight

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.030
on the importance of
effective communication

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.960
over the phone between
businesses and consumers.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.080
So today, I'll start off
by sharing a pain point

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.440
we identified in
those communications

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.380
and how we went about
developing a solution around it.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.840
And then I'll turn
it to Stephen,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:30.130
in who will explain how we
work with leading partners

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:34.090
in order to solve these few
pain points to as many users

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.840
and as many
businesses as we can.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.230
When we look at the data, we
see that the average person

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.060
receives 30 spam
calls each month.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.720
And over 2019, there
was a sizable increase

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.140
in phone calls.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.320
The vast majority
of businesses feel

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.020
outbound calls are important
for them to meet their customer

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.700
service calls.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.140
But here's the problem.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.640
Like me, most consumers simply
don't answer their phone

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.990
if they don't
recognize the number.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:10.259
So there is a massive gap in the
perceived importance of calls

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:12.570
and their actual
effectiveness, which is low

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.760
because people don't answer.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.570
So how did we reach this stage?

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.660
Today, any device that is
connected to the internet

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.800
is capable of making
voice calls through VOIP.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.990
This means that the
good old caller ID

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.740
system which displays the
caller [INAUDIBLE] number

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.300
can be spoofed very easily.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.490
There's no trust in the system.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.220
So in practice, a
person that sits

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.790
in the other side of the world
can make a call to my phone,

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.450
and it will look like--

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:48.360
as similar as a call from
my local bank number.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:53.530
So why would consumers
trust phone calls anymore?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:56.470
This brings us to
verified calls.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.970
Being helpful and provide a
trust experience for users

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.380
is at core with what
we do at Google.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.540
And on the left
of the screen, you

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.820
can see how a business
call looks today.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.490
At best, it's an
unidentified call--

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.030
nothing personal.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.250
It's just a phone number.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.470
It doesn't mean
anything to the user.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.240
And it looks very similar
to a spam call I receive

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.630
or the bank call I missed.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.500
They look exactly the same.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.082
Next you'll see how
verified calls look like.

00:03:30.082 --> 00:03:33.449
[RINGTONE]

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.370
So let's walk through
the experience.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:44.120
On the top, we've got a blue
badge with a verified checkmark

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.010
and we also display the
name and logo of the brand,

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.610
so the user can
know who's calling.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:54.500
Finally, we allow the user to
state the reason for calling.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.310
And think-- just think
about how wonderful

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.960
it would have been if
my bank could show,

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.820
hey, this is me calling.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.920
And this is the reason,
about the potential fraud

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.030
in your account.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.700
I would obviously pick this
phone call up in a second.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.180
And as you can see, we
included all of the information

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.920
that consumers value in order
to make sure we set the call up

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.890
for an engaging and productive
communication between the two

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:21.500
sides.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.670
So we call this
product Verified Calls.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:30.200
So I want to you walk you
through what verified means.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.420
For one, it signals that
the business has passed

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.100
Google's verification process.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.620
It also validates that
the call is coming

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.200
for a the number is showing.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.240
In other words,
it's not spoofed.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.300
And finally, it gives
the user the information

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.670
they need, including
the reason for calling,

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:52.480
so they can make an
informed decision.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.330
Let me walk you through
the verification process.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.485
We use an out-of-band
channel to verify the calls,

00:04:58.485 --> 00:04:59.860
meaning that the
phone call still

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.120
goes through regular
channels without any change,

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:08.330
and the verification is done
separately through an API.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.060
And to make it even
easier for brands to join,

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:15.320
we work with selected telephony
providers to integrate the API

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.200
and perform the verification,
and this minimize the friction

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.070
for brands to join.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:26.060
The first step is to query
the API for reachability data,

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.000
and make sure the phone number
can deliver a Verified Calls

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.630
experience.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.760
Once this is done,
the next step is

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.670
to send Google the brand phone
number, the consumer phone

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.410
number, and the call reason, and
Google syncs this information

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.650
with the device.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.400
And once the voice
call arrives, the user

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.470
will see the Verified Calls UI.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:51.700
And now I'm excited to share
with you our demo, which

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:57.000
you can see how easy it is
to get your calls verified.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.250
To verify a call,
the first step is

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.910
to check if the phone
number is reachable.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.730
As you can see, I
received a response

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.350
that the device is
indeed reachable.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.380
So I can continue
to the next step

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.510
and send the verified
call's information.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.300
Since I received a 200
response from the server,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.270
I know my data was
saved, and I can go ahead

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.380
and make a regular phone call.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.181
And the phone call
will be verified.

00:06:24.181 --> 00:06:27.618
[RINGTONE]

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.080
Without going into
too many details,

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.210
I'll just say that
our services are

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.890
powered by the great
infrastructure of Google Cloud.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:43.310
And I will end my
section by mentioning

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:46.850
that we have designed this
API with our users' privacy

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:51.650
in mind, and Google removes
any personal information

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.540
after the verification
is complete.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.260
Now, I am happy
to turn this over

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:01.760
to Steve, that will show
you how we are partnering

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:05.733
with businesses and share their
tremendous interest we've seen.

00:07:05.733 --> 00:07:06.900
STEPHEN BROUGH: Thanks, Gal.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.660
As you recall from the
beginning of the presentation,

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.560
87% of consumers don't answer
calls from unknown numbers.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.290
This is particularly a
problem for urgent calls,

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.480
like Gal's case with his bank.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.510
By verifying the caller with
the logo and other details

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.640
like call reason,
our research shows

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:26.310
we can make calls
more trustworthy,

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.830
communicate the
relevance to the user,

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:32.680
and ultimately
improve answering.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.330
For the launch of
Verified Calls,

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.310
Google has partnered
with leading providers,

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.260
like the ones on
this page, to make

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:41.440
calls more trustworthy and
relevant for consumers.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.530
For the latest on all partners
supporting Verified Calls,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.620
please visit the website below.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:51.450
Our focus on making business
to consumer communications more

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.960
trustworthy and engaging
doesn't stop at voice calls.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.790
Back in December 2019, we
publicly launched Verified SMS.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.810
Similar to how Verified Calls
enhances calling experiences,

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:06.570
Verified SMS makes
business SMS messaging

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:10.470
safer and more trustworthy
by adding sender verification

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.080
and brand.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:16.830
Many brands, like
1-800-Flowers, Kayak,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.560
and Google Pay are
already sending messages

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.320
with verified SMS, which
is live across nine

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.085
countries, including the US and
Canada in North America, Brazil

00:08:26.085 --> 00:08:31.200
and Mexico in South America,
UK, Spain, and France in Europe,

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.299
and India and the
Philippines in Asia.

00:08:35.299 --> 00:08:37.929
And we have more
countries planned in 2020.

00:08:37.929 --> 00:08:39.760
For more information
on this service,

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.179
please visit the link below.

00:08:43.179 --> 00:08:46.150
When we started down this path
of creating both Verified SMS

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.270
and Verified Calls we expected
verified communications

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.570
to be valuable to both
businesses and users.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:56.050
In a recent user
sentiment survey in the US

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.630
and in Brazil for
verified SMS, we

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.370
tested this assumption
and the feedback

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:03.440
was overwhelmingly positive.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.160
In that same survey, we were
both positively surprised

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:10.760
to see how strong user sentiment
was across the customer

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:16.560
lifecycle, particularly areas
that influenced new and repeat

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.190
business, like
business consideration,

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:24.557
likelihood to purchase, and
likelihood to recommend.

00:09:24.557 --> 00:09:26.640
While we haven't conducted
the same user sentiment

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.850
survey for Verified Calls
given how new it is,

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:31.920
anecdotal evidence from
partner discussions

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.470
give us confidence that
sentiment will be equally

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.380
strong for this service, too.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.380
Verified Calls is first
available in these five

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.460
countries--

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:46.900
US, Mexico and Brazil in the
Americas, Spain in Europe,

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.800
and India in Asia, with more
countries planned in 2020.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.060
The Google Phone app
and Verified Calls

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.440
comes preloaded on many Android
devices in these markets,

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:03.410
including ones from
Motorola, Nokia, Xiaomi,

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.120
OnePlus, and, of course, Pixel.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.490
However, if you don't
already have the Google Phone

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:12.210
app on your Android
phone, that's OK.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.700
Coming soon, you'll
be able to download it

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.770
from the Play Store.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.010
For partners and
businesses wanting

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.990
to take advantage
of Verified Calls,

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.090
it's simple to get started.

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:25.790
Just register your
interest in the website,

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.660
or email us directly
for more information.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:31.210
Thank you for joining
Gal and i today

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:34.780
to hear how Verified Calls makes
business calls safer and more

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.010
purposeful.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.070
Have a great day.

